==English==

===Alternative forms===
* [[criticise]] (''UK'')

===Etymology===
Century 1911: from {{suffix|critic|ize|lang=en}}

From {{etyl|grc|en}} {{term|κριτικός||of or for judging, able to discern|tr=kritikos|lang=grc}}, from {{term|κρίσις||crisis|tr=krisis|lang=grc}}

===Verb===
{{en-verb|criticiz}}  (''transitive'' or ''intransitive'')

# to [[find fault]] (with something)
# to [[evaluate]] (something), and [[judge]] its [[merit]]s and [[fault]]s

